"""Operation-specific public contracts for the identity transaction family."""

OPERATION_CONTRACTS = {
    "idtx-generation-slot-pool": "The constructor creates max(capacity,0) empty slots, each at generation 1. acquire scans increasing slot indexes, stores any integer payload, and returns that slot and generation, or nullopt when full. release and resolve accept only an in-range live handle with the exact current generation; release clears it and increments generation, skipping zero on wrap. Invalid or stale handles return false/nullopt.",
    "idtx-monotonic-tombstone-registry": "create rejects an empty name or an exhausted LLONG_MAX frontier with -1; otherwise it returns the next positive ID starting at 1 and advances permanently. retire and rename require a live ID, and rename also requires a nonempty name. lookup returns only live names. reset_active retires every live ID but never rewinds next_, so retired IDs are never reissued.",
    "idtx-block-lease-allocator": "A positive count creates one half-open free block [first,first+count); a nonpositive count creates none. lease(length) rejects length<=0, chooses the lowest-begin first block large enough, removes an exact fit or leaves its right remainder, and returns {begin,length}; exhaustion returns nullopt. release requires an exact live lease and coalesces adjacent free blocks on both sides. free_blocks is begin-sorted.",
    "idtx-worker-epoch-id": "workers must be positive and sequence_bits must be in [1,30] for next/decode to succeed. For worker w in [0,workers) and nonnegative epoch e not below that worker's last epoch, sequence starts at 0 on a newer epoch and is bounded by L=2^sequence_bits. next returns ((e*workers)+w)*L+sequence, then increments; regression or exhaustion returns nullopt unchanged. decode(id>=0) returns epoch=(id/L)/workers, worker=(id/L)%workers, sequence=id%L; invalid configuration or negative ID returns nullopt.",
    "idtx-hierarchical-scope-id": "The initial tree contains only root with next sequence 1. add_scope requires a nonempty new child other than root and an existing parent. allocate requires an existing scope and returns scope+'#'+its next positive sequence. erase_scope rejects root/unknown, recursively removes that scope and descendants, invalidates exactly their IDs, and detaches them from surviving parents. valid reports membership in the remaining live-ID set.",
    "idtx-content-probe-id": "A positive modulus defines IDs [0,modulus); otherwise intern always fails. digest is 32-bit FNV-1a (offset 2166136261, xor each unsigned byte, multiply 16777619). intern rejects empty payload, starts at digest%modulus, probes +1 circularly at most modulus slots, returns an existing ID for equal payload, inserts at first empty ID, and never overwrites an unequal collision. payload returns nullopt for unoccupied IDs.",
    "idtx-dense-handle-table": "insert appends {next positive handle,value}, records its dense index, and never reuses a handle. erase rejects unknown handles; otherwise it moves the final dense entry into the erased index when needed, repairs that moved handle's sparse index, then removes the old tail and handle. get resolves through the sparse index. dense_values returns current dense order, including swap-remove reordering.",
    "idtx-interval-id-leases": "grant accepts owner>0 and begin<end only when half-open [begin,end) overlaps no lease; touching endpoints are allowed. release requires one existing lease of the same owner that fully contains [begin,end), rejects empty/outside/wrong-owner ranges, removes that subrange, and emits left/right residual leases when nonempty. leases returns all {begin,end,owner} tuples ordered by begin.",
    "idtx-namespace-quota-ids": "add_namespace requires a nonempty unique name and quota>0. allocate requires an existing namespace below quota, returns name+':'+the namespace's positive monotonic sequence, increments active and sequence only on success, and otherwise nullopt. release requires an exact live generated ID and decrements its owner once. active returns -1 for an unknown namespace and its current count otherwise.",
    "idtx-epoch-sequence-book": "advance requires epoch strictly greater than the current epoch; success clears every per-stream sequence and live token. issue requires a nonempty stream and positive current epoch, starts that stream at sequence 1, advances until an unused {epoch,sequence}, records it, and returns it. live is true only for a recorded token whose epoch equals the current epoch. Failed advance/issue changes nothing.",
    "idtx-partition-stride-ids": "A positive partition count creates one next value per partition, initialized to its index. next accepts partition in [0,partitions), returns its current value, then adds the partition count; invalid configuration/index returns nullopt. reconfigure accepts a positive count only before any ID was issued and reinitializes progressions; after issuance it returns false unchanged. issued returns IDs in issue order.",
    "idtx-capability-token-pool": "mint requires resource>0 and sequence below UINT_MAX; it returns (epoch<<32)|sequence, starting epoch/sequence at 1, records the resource, and increments sequence. revoke succeeds once for a live token and removes its authority. authorize returns the live resource only. rotate_epoch invalidates all tokens, increments epoch while skipping zero, and restarts sequence at 1, so no prior observed token is reissued.",
    "idtx-reversible-id-stack": "allocate returns increasing positive IDs, logs them, and marks them live. checkpoint is the allocation-log length. rollback rejects tokens past the log; otherwise it removes the suffix IDs from live state and resets the frontier to one after the last retained allocation (or 1 when empty). release succeeds only for a currently live ID and does not alter log/frontier. live returns IDs in ascending set order.",
    "idtx-reserved-band-allocator": "reserve_band requires nonempty unique name, begin<end, and no overlap with any existing half-open band. allocate requires a known nonempty band, normalizes hint into that band, circularly scans every band ID from the hint, reserves the first unused, or returns nullopt when full. release requires the named band and an ID currently used in it. Allocation never crosses band boundaries.",
    "idtx-alias-component-ids": "add accepts a positive new ID as a singleton and increments components. alias requires two known distinct components, unions by rank, and on equal rank chooses the smaller root ID, increments its rank, and decrements components; unknown or already-equal inputs return false. canonical returns the current root or nullopt for unknown. components reports singleton/component count.",
    "idtx-robin-hood-key-registry": "A positive capacity creates an empty table; keys must be nonnegative and unique. home=key%capacity. insert linearly probes, swapping with an occupant whose probe distance is smaller, and fails atomically after a full cycle. get stops at empty or an occupant distance below the search distance. erase rejects absent keys, backward-shifts the following cluster until empty/home, decrementing every moved distance. probe_distances follows physical slot order.",
    "idtx-cuckoo-route-registry": "A positive capacity creates two equal tables. Keys must be nonnegative and unique; h1=key%capacity and h2=(unsigned(key)*2654435761)%capacity. route searches both tables. insert works on copies, alternates h1/h2 displacement for at most 2*capacity moves, commits both tables only when an empty home is reached, and otherwise returns false with both live tables unchanged.",
    "idtx-quadratic-ticket-table": "A positive capacity creates empty slots. place rejects negative/duplicate tickets and probes positions (ticket%capacity+i*i)%capacity for i=0..capacity-1, storing at the first empty position and returning it; no reachable empty returns nullopt unchanged. contains uses the same complete bounded quadratic sequence and reports exact ticket equality.",
    "idtx-hopscotch-neighborhood-index": "capacity and neighborhood must be positive and keys nonnegative/unique. A key's home is key%capacity and it must finish at circular offset <neighborhood. insert finds the first free slot, repeatedly relocates an earlier occupant that remains within its own neighborhood until the free slot enters the new key's neighborhood, and fails unchanged if no move exists. contains scans only the home neighborhood; offsets lists occupied offsets there.",
    "idtx-double-hash-session-table": "prime_capacity must exceed 1. For nonnegative ID k, first=k%capacity and step=1+k%(capacity-1); open and slot probe first+n*step modulo capacity for at most capacity positions. open rejects invalid/duplicate/full and writes the first empty slot; slot returns the exact occupied position or nullopt, stopping at the first empty position.",
    "idtx-shortest-prefix-aliases": "add accepts a nonempty unique exact name; erase succeeds only for a present exact name. alias requires a present name and returns its shortest nonempty prefix that is not a prefix of any other present name, testing lengths from 1 upward; if no shorter prefix is unique it returns the whole name. Results are computed from current membership, so erase may shorten aliases.",
    "idtx-checksum-bucket-ledger": "checksum is the sum of unsigned key bytes modulo 17. append rejects empty or duplicate full keys, then appends {key,value} to that checksum bucket. lookup scans only the computed bucket but compares the complete key, returning its value or nullopt. bucket(checksum) returns keys in append order; distinct colliding keys remain distinct.",
    "idtx-coordinate-cell-reservations": "The grid contains rows*cols cells with valid coordinates 0<=row<rows, 0<=col<cols. reserve rejects an invalid request, then chooses the unused cell minimizing Manhattan distance to the request, breaking ties by smaller row then column, records and returns it, or nullopt when full. release succeeds only for the exact currently reserved cell.",
    "idtx-interval-code-bookings": "book requires code>0, begin<end, a new code, and no positive-length overlap with any existing half-open interval; touching endpoints are allowed. Success records [begin,end). cancel removes a present code once. interval returns the exact recorded pair or nullopt. Every rejected booking/cancel leaves all bookings unchanged.",
    "idtx-dependency-name-resolver": "add accepts a nonempty new canonical name resolving to itself. bind_alias requires a nonempty alias, existing target, and alias!=target; it may create/replace an alias only if following links remains acyclic, otherwise it restores the prior graph. resolve follows links to a self-root and returns it, or nullopt for unknown/cyclic input. Failed binding changes nothing.",
    "idtx-priority-slot-displacement": "A positive slot count creates empty slots and order 0. claim requires id>0, desired in range, and a globally new ID. It probes circularly from desired on a copy; a strictly higher-priority moving claim displaces a lower one and continues after that slot, while equal/lower priority probes onward, preserving earlier ties. It commits only if every displaced claim is placed, returns the new ID's slot, and then increments order. at returns nullopt out of range.",
    "idtx-canonical-slug-registry": "canonicalization scans unsigned bytes: alphanumeric bytes are lowercased; each maximal non-alphanumeric run becomes one hyphen only between alphanumeric groups; leading/trailing separators vanish. reserve rejects an empty canonical result, returns the base if unused, otherwise tries base+'-'+n for n=2 through 999999 and returns the first unused or nullopt. An explicit suffixed input is canonicalized as its own base. release removes only an exact reserved slug once.",
    "idtx-batch-matching-identities": "assign rejects any request with id<=0, empty acceptable list, or duplicate request ID. Nonnegative slot choices form a bipartite graph. Requests are processed by ascending ID with augmenting-path reassignment of earlier owners; success returns the complete id->slot matching, while any unmatched request returns nullopt with no partial map.",
    "idtx-displacement-chain-names": "insert rejects empty/duplicate names. Empty displaces appends; otherwise displaces must name an existing element and the new name is inserted immediately before it on a copy. moved is the count of positions among the old/new common prefix whose value changes. Commit only when moved<=limit; otherwise return false with order unchanged. order returns the current vector.",
    "idtx-collision-journal-replay": "slots defines valid requested/assigned positions [0,slots). insert rejects empty key, invalid request, duplicate key, or full table; it circularly scans from requested, assigns first free position, appends exactly {key,requested,assigned}, and returns assigned. replay reconstructs from empty state and succeeds only if every computed assignment equals the supplied one; then it atomically replaces state/journal, otherwise preserves both. journal returns recorded order.",
    "idtx-generation-stamped-counters": "A positive size creates zero counters tagged stale. add requires a valid index and amount>=0; on the first access in the current generation it retags and zeroes the cell, then adds. get returns -1 for invalid index, zero for a stale generation, otherwise its value. reset advances the generation in O(1); on unsigned wrap it material-clears cells and restarts generation at 1.",
    "idtx-lazy-epoch-membership": "A positive key count creates untagged keys at epoch 1. include requires an in-range key and tags it current. contains is true exactly for an in-range key with current tag. next_epoch increments the byte epoch and normally returns false; on wrap it clears all tags, sets epoch to 1, and returns true so old epoch-1 membership cannot revive.",
    "idtx-snapshot-state-restore": "set requires a nonempty key, writes its value, and returns 1 (empty returns 0). snapshot stores an immutable full state under increasing positive ID and returns it. restore requires a known snapshot, then replaces the entire state including deleting keys absent from it; unknown returns false unchanged. get returns current value or nullopt.",
    "idtx-delta-checkpoint-rewind": "add requires nonempty key and nonzero delta, adds it, and appends the exact delta. checkpoint is log length. rewind rejects a token past the log; otherwise it pops the suffix in reverse, subtracts each delta, and erases keys whose value becomes zero. value returns zero for absent keys. Rewind to the current token is a successful no-op.",
    "idtx-namespace-selective-reset": "put requires a nonempty dot-separated path and stores/replaces its value. get returns exact-path value or nullopt. reset(prefix) requires nonempty prefix and removes paths equal to prefix or starting prefix+'.', never mere textual siblings such as 'ab' for 'a'; it returns the number removed and preserves all other paths.",
    "idtx-expiry-lease-reset": "grant requires id>0, deadline>=current time, and a new live ID; it creates generation 1 and queues an event. renew requires a live ID and deadline>=now, increments generation and queues a new event. advance rejects time regression by returning empty unchanged; otherwise it updates now, pops events with deadline<=now, and expires/returns IDs only when event generation/deadline still matches the live lease, ordered by deadline then ID.",
    "idtx-cohort-barrier-reset": "The constructor owns the exact nonempty/empty member set. arrive rejects a nonmember or duplicate arrival. A nonfinal distinct member is recorded and returns nullopt. The final missing member clears arrivals, increments generation, and returns the new generation. generation starts 0 and reports completed cohorts; an empty cohort accepts nobody.",
    "idtx-rolling-window-reset": "width must be positive. record requires nondecreasing time and value>=0, appends {time,value}, and advances last time. reset requires nondecreasing time, clears all values, and advances last time. sum requires nondecreasing now, removes entries with time<=now-width (the window is (now-width,now]), and returns their sum; invalid width/time returns false or -1 unchanged.",
    "idtx-recovery-fsm-reset": "Initial state is healthy. fault(code>0) succeeds only from healthy and records code. acknowledge succeeds only from faulted with the exact code. begin_test succeeds only from acknowledged. test_result succeeds only from testing: pass returns healthy and clears code; failure returns faulted retaining code. Every out-of-order/mismatched call returns false unchanged; state reports the enum.",
    "idtx-sequence-gap-resync": "next starts at the constructor baseline. receive rejects sequence<next or duplicate buffered sequence; otherwise it buffers value. drain repeatedly removes and returns values for contiguous keys starting at next, advancing next, and stops at the first gap. resync requires baseline>=next, sets next, and discards only buffered sequences below it; higher buffered values remain available for later drain.",
    "idtx-tombstone-compaction-reset": "Positive capacity creates open-address slots with empty/live/tombstone state and monotonic insertion order. insert rejects negative/duplicate/full, linearly probes key%capacity, remembers the first tombstone, and uses it before a later empty. erase marks an exact live key tombstone. compact rebuilds all live keys into a clean same-size table while preserving their order numbers; iteration returns live keys sorted by insertion order.",
    "idtx-quota-period-reset": "width and quota must be positive for admission. Times must be nondecreasing. Period start is globally aligned as floor(time/width)*width; crossing or landing exactly on a later boundary resets used to zero and updates start. admit succeeds and increments while used<quota, otherwise false unchanged. used and period_start expose current window state.",
    "idtx-deterministic-seed-reset": "State starts at the supplied seed, except zero is normalized to 1. next applies xorshift steps state^=state<<13, state^=state>>7, state^=state<<17, increments draws, and returns the low unsigned bits. reset applies the same seed normalization and sets draws to zero, so equal seeds reproduce the stream. draws reports calls since construction/reset.",
    "idtx-hierarchy-cascade-reset": "add requires a nonempty new node and every listed dependency already present; duplicate/unknown input fails unchanged. reset requires a known root and returns a deterministic postorder DFS: each dependency in stored vector order before its dependent, with a shared dependency emitted once. Unknown root returns nullopt.",
    "idtx-rollback-union-find-reset": "A positive size creates size singleton components indexed [0,size). checkpoint is undo-log length. unite rejects invalid/already-connected nodes, attaches smaller tree under larger (argument-order root wins equal size), logs child/root prior size, and decrements components. No path compression is allowed. rollback rejects future token, otherwise reverses log suffix restoring parents/sizes/components. connected rejects invalid via false.",
    "idtx-undo-log-kv": "begin succeeds only when inactive and starts an empty undo/logged set without clearing base data. During an active transaction, the first set/erase per nonempty key logs its exact prior optional value; set writes and erase requires presence. commit requires active and discards undo. abort requires active and replays before-images in reverse, restoring present values or erasing newly created keys. get reads current data.",
    "idtx-write-ahead-ledger": "prepare rejects an empty write set or empty keys with -1; otherwise it stores an uncommitted record under increasing positive ID without applying data. commit requires a known uncommitted record, marks it committed, and applies its writes in vector order once. crash_recover clears data then replays every committed record in increasing record ID, skipping prepared-only records. get returns value/nullopt.",
    "idtx-mvcc-snapshot-store": "snapshot returns the current global version, initially 0. commit requires nonempty key, increments version, and appends {version,value} to that key's chain. read rejects negative/future snapshots or absent/no-version-at-or-before key; otherwise it returns the value with greatest version<=snapshot. Later commits never affect earlier snapshot reads.",
    "idtx-optimistic-version-batch": "seed requires nonempty new key and stores {value,version=1}. commit requires every Read key once, present, and at exactly supplied version; every Write key must be nonempty. After all validation, writes apply on a copy in order, replacing value and incrementing existing version or creating version 1. Any failed read/write validation aborts every write. get returns {value,version} or nullopt.",
    "idtx-lock-order-transfer": "add requires account>0, opening>=0, and uniqueness. transfer requires distinct known accounts, amount>0, and sufficient source balance. Success appends lock plan {min(from,to),max(from,to)} then debits/credits; all failures append no plan and mutate no balance. balance returns nullopt unknown; lock_plans preserves successful transfer order.",
    "idtx-two-phase-resource-commit": "add requires nonempty unique participant and capacity>=0. transact(empty) returns -1. For nonempty demand, every participant must exist, amount>=0, and used+amount<=capacity; any no-vote returns 0 and changes none. If all vote yes, all used counts increase and result is 1. used returns zero for unknown or the committed usage.",
    "idtx-savepoint-stack-store": "begin succeeds only when inactive and starts a transaction. savepoint requires active, returns an increasing ID, and records current undo position. set requires active/nonempty key, logs each before-image and writes. rollback_to requires a live savepoint, reverses changes after it, retains that savepoint, and discards later savepoints. release succeeds only for the top savepoint. commit requires active and keeps data while clearing transactional metadata. get accepts any string, returns the currently visible stored value for a present key, returns nullopt for an absent key, does not require an active transaction, and never mutates state.",
    "idtx-nested-transaction-map": "set rejects empty key; outside a transaction it writes base, otherwise top overlay. begin pushes an empty overlay. get searches overlays newest to oldest then base. commit/abort require depth>0: commit pops and merges the child into its parent overlay or base; abort discards only the child. Thus child commit remains abortable by an outer parent. depth is overlay count.",
    "idtx-escrow-counter-transaction": "add_partition requires id>0, rights>=0, and uniqueness. transfer_rights requires distinct known partitions, amount>0, and sufficient local source rights, then atomically moves rights. spend requires amount>0 and sufficient rights in that exact partition, decrements them, and increments global spent. rights returns -1 unknown; spent is total successful spend.",
    "idtx-atomic-batch-rename": "add requires nonempty unique name. rename requires a nonempty mapping whose every source exists, names are nonempty, destinations are unique, and any occupied destination is also a source in the same batch. It snapshots all source values, removes all sources, then installs destinations atomically, so cycles/swaps work. Any invalid mapping leaves data unchanged. get returns value/nullopt.",
    "idtx-double-entry-transfer": "add_account requires id>0, opening>=0, uniqueness. transfer requires positive unused transaction ID, distinct known accounts, amount>0, and sufficient source. Success records exactly debit {tx,from,-amount} then credit {tx,to,+amount}, marks tx used, and mutates balances; failure records/mutates nothing. balance is optional; entries returns matching journal entries in journal order.",
    "idtx-inventory-reservation-commit": "stock requires nonempty unique item and count>=0. reserve rejects empty request, nonpositive quantity, unknown item, or insufficient quantity with -1 before any debit; success debits all items, stores request under increasing positive ID, and returns it. commit removes a held reservation without restoring stock. release restores all held quantities then removes it. Unknown commit/release false; available unknown -1.",
    "idtx-dependency-dag-transaction": "add_node requires positive unique ID. add_edges rejects empty input; every edge must connect known distinct nodes and be new within a copied graph. The complete staged graph must be acyclic; only then it replaces live graph and increments revision once. Invalid/cyclic batches leave graph/revision unchanged. reachable requires known endpoints and includes zero-length self reachability; revision starts 0.",
    "idtx-idempotency-key-ledger": "execute requires nonempty key and payload. A new key records payload and Result{status=200,value=input*2}, increments executions, and returns it. Reusing the key with identical payload returns the first stored result regardless of new value and does not execute again; different payload returns nullopt unchanged. executions counts distinct successful new keys.",
    "idtx-saga-compensation-runner": "run rejects empty steps, nonpositive IDs, or duplicate IDs with nullopt. It visits in vector order. Successful steps append ID to forward. If all succeed, committed=true and compensated empty. At the first failing step, that ID and later steps are not forward-executed; committed=false and compensated is exactly completed forward IDs in reverse, once each.",
}


